From ffa8dedfca0e11050653f16db96f84a1634a69aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "xen/ioreq: Do not let bufioreq to be used on other
 than x86 arches" for the RPi5 virtio-pci device-model

Upstream commit 2fbd7e609e1 (Oleksandr Tyshchenko) made
ioreq_server_create() reject any non-x86 ioreq server that requests
buffered I/O (bufioreq_handling != 0), with the rationale that "there
is no caller which requires to send buffered I/O request on Arm".

That premise does not hold for this disaggregated demo: the DomD
device-model (qemu, hw/xen/xen_common.h:xen_create_ioreq_server())
unconditionally passes HVM_IOREQSRV_BUFIOREQ_ATOMIC when creating its
ioreq server for the DomU/DomA virtio-pci backends. On 4.19 the
xen-troops fork carried this revert, so create_ioreq_server() accepted
the ATOMIC request and the device-model came up (the buffered ioreq
page is allocated but unused on Arm, which is harmless). The revert was
lost during the 4.21 (xen-4.21-xt-gen5) rebase, so the same qemu now
gets -EINVAL from create_ioreq_server() -> the device-model exits ->
the guest PCIe host bridge (pcie.0) is never created -> "Bus 'pcie.0'
not found" -> DomU/DomA stay black.

Re-apply the 4.19 behaviour by dropping the Arm bufioreq rejection. The
remaining `bufioreq_handling > HVM_IOREQSRV_BUFIOREQ_ATOMIC` range check
is kept.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [intentional downstream revert of upstream hardening 2fbd7e609e -- re-permits bufioreq on Arm for this virtio-heavy disaggregated config; a deliberate security relaxation for the demo, not for upstream (upstream keeps the restriction)]
---
 xen/common/ioreq.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xen/common/ioreq.c b/xen/common/ioreq.c
index f5fd30ce12..7f7dd9459a 100644
--- a/xen/common/ioreq.c
+++ b/xen/common/ioreq.c
@@ -647,9 +647,6 @@ static int ioreq_server_create(struct domain *d, int bufioreq_handling,
     unsigned int i;
     int rc;
 
-    if ( !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_X86) && bufioreq_handling )
-        return -EINVAL;
-
     if ( bufioreq_handling > HVM_IOREQSRV_BUFIOREQ_ATOMIC )
         return -EINVAL;

--
2.34.1
